From 963a4fa7c03e2135ffe04a6b9aea2948d3389663 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:55:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Input: choose which key groups reach Android Auto

A head unit's key handler often delivers presses that were never meant
for the projection. On cars whose factory system keeps the steering
wheel (an Audi MMI, for one), the wheel's OK still reaches this app and
Android Auto selects something the driver never looked at. Bindings
could not help: an unbound key goes on as itself, and the media setting
covers next, previous and play/pause only.

Settings > Input > Send Keys To Android Auto: a multi-choice of key
groups, all ticked by default so nothing changes until a user unticks
one: OK / Select, Arrows and rotary knob, Back, Call and hang up, Voice
assistant, Keyboard and other keys.

- Stored as the groups held back, so an unset preference, and any group
  added later, sends everything.
- Unbound keys only: a key bound in the keymap names its Android Auto key
  on purpose and is always sent as bound; gestures never pass here.
- Media keys stay with Send Media Buttons To Android Auto, volume with
  Send Volume Buttons To The Phone; neither is affected. The media
  setting's hint, which said the other keys always reach Android Auto,
  now points to the new setting.
- A held-back press is logged with its group.

AaKeyGroupPolicy is pure and unit-tested; AaKeyGroupsDialogTest shows
the choice in all 26 locales on a portrait phone and an 800x450 unit and
checks no group's name is cut.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WfvDdsw9pz4kqjTjiNxyCC
